meta {
  name: 16 Import Lab Tests into Branch
  type: http
  seq: 13
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/branch-lab-tests/import
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{operatorToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "labTestIds": ["{{labTestIdA}}", "{{labTestIdB}}", "{{labTestIdC}}"]
  }
}

docs {
  **Catalogue 16 — Import ALL THREE member lab tests into the branch** (the default
  Walk-in list). Deep-copies each master-data lab test (with its result parameters)
  into the branch as a branch-owned snapshot. Doing this BEFORE the panel import
  matters: the panel import (step 20) **reuses** these three branch lab tests as its
  members (matched by source id), so the panel's `memberBranchLabTestId`s equal the
  `branchLabTestIdA`/`branchLabTestIdB`/`branchLabTestIdC` resolved next — the exact
  ids the adapter is mapped on in step 27. The branch lab test ids are resolved in
  17/18/18c.
}
